{"title":"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_23\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 23</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solutions</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_23\">Problem 23</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 23\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From a regular octagon, a triangle is formed by connecting three randomly chosen vertices of the octagon. What is the probability that at least one of the sides of the triangle is also a side of the octagon?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d911c096b9c5403a914f8b8c2b05b4915494f1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(3cm); pair A[]; for (int i=0; i&lt;9; ++i) {   A[i] = rotate(22.5+45*i)*(1,0); } filldraw(A[0]--A[1]--A[2]--A[3]--A[4]--A[5]--A[6]--A[7]--cycle,gray,black); for (int i=0; i&lt;8; ++i) { dot(A[i]); } [/asy]\" width=\"145\" height=\"145\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/0/5d0b3c02aafe778f2d092bd57c8ba8ce04ef7bd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } \\frac{2}{7} \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } \\frac{5}{42} \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } \\frac{11}{14} \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } \\frac{5}{7} \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } \\frac{6}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"390\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Firstly, we calculate the amount of all possible triangles. It is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/f/86fd9b077697558ac8ba1a59078a3e50f89a77ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_8^3=56$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"66\" height=\"21\" />. Then, we consider how many triangles have at least a edge which is also the edge of octagon. \n</p><p>If the triangle shares only one edge with the octagon, fix an edge, we can choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> different vertices for the triangle. Thus, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/9/7c9c2ba2d6fe09acb7b2fe6dce53953090141536.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8\\times 4=32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> possible triangles. If the triangle shares its two edges with the octagon, obviously, there are only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible triangles. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/9/bf9efb1d211b099434b4abed9b43aa0e7fd3075f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{32+8}{56}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\frac{5}{7}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"133\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We split into two cases:\n</p><p>Case 1: Exactly one side is chosen.  \nThere are 4 lines that each contain 1 side of the octagon, and there are 8 points on the octagon. Thus, the total number of such lines is:\n\\begin{align}\n8 \\cdot 4 &amp;= 32.\n\\end{align}\n</p><p>Case 2: Exactly two sides are chosen.  \nThe number of ways to choose 2 points on the octagon is:\n\\begin{align}\n\\binom{8}{1} &amp;= 8.\n\\end{align}\n</p><p>Adding the results from both cases, the total is:\n\\begin{align}\n32 + 8 &amp;= \\boxed{40}.\n\\end{align}\n</p><p>This is the numerator. To find the denominator we do <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/f/86fd9b077697558ac8ba1a59078a3e50f89a77ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_8^3=56$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"66\" height=\"21\" />. Thus, our final answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab834c1ec652bcaacc8aad469c90db5994aa01d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${40/56= \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\frac{5}{7}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"125\" height=\"49\" />. \n</p><p>-jb2015007\n</p><p>-FrankensteinQuixoteCabin\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/5UojVH4Cqqs?t=2678\">https://youtu.be/5UojVH4Cqqs?t=2678</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solutions\">Video Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VNflxl7VpL0\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VNflxl7VpL0</a>\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/YeYDixFXsvA\">https://youtu.be/YeYDixFXsvA</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8\" title=\"2018 AMC 8\">2018 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.p